The '''2026–27 EFL Cup''' is the 67th and current season of the [[EFL Cup|English Football League Cup]].<ref name="si_mag">{{Cite magazine |author=McCormack, James|title=2026–27 Carabao Cup: Draw, Fixtures, Results and Guide to Each Round |url=https://www.si.com/soccer/2026-27-carabao-cup-draw-fixtures-results-guide-each-round |magazine=[[Sports Illustrated]]|date=9 September 2026 |access-date=20 September 2026 |language=en-us}}</ref> It is sponsored by [[Carabao Energy Drink]] and known as the '''Carabao Cup''' for sponsorship reasons,<ref>{{cite web |author=Williams, Callum |title=Carabao to launch Carabao Lager in UK after securing EFL title rights |url=https://insidersport.com/2026/03/16/carabao-cup-efl-extension-lager-launch/ |website=insidersport.com |publisher=Sports Betting Community Ltd |date=16 March 2026 |access-date=19 September 2026}}</ref> with the 2026–27 season marking the tenth season of Carabao's sponsorship of the competition.<ref>{{cite web |author=Ewing, Harry |title=Carabao renew EFL Cup title sponsorship for further three seasons |url=https://www.insideworldfootball.com/2023/10/18/carabao-renew-efl-cup-title-sponsorship-three-seasons/ |publisher=Inside World Football |date=18 October 2023 |access-date=21 September 2026 }}</ref> The EFL Cup is open to all clubs participating in the [[Premier League]] and the [[English Football League]].<ref name="all_clubs"/>

The preliminary round began on 1 August 2026, followed by the tournament proper on 7 August 2026.<ref name="Round_One"/> This season's EFL Cup final will be held at [[Wembley Stadium]] on Sunday, 21 March 2027, marking the 20th consecutive year that the venue has hosted the competition's final.<ref name="si_mag"/>

[[Manchester City F.C.|Manchester City]] are the defending champions, having beaten [[Arsenal F.C.|Arsenal]] in the [[2026 EFL Cup final|previous season's final]].<ref>{{cite news |author=Hytner, David |title=Manchester City win Carabao Cup after Nico O’Reilly’s double downs lacklustre Arsenal |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/mar/22/arsenal-manchester-city-carabao-cup-final-match-report |work=[[The Guardian]] |publisher=Guardian Media Group |date=22 March 2026 |access-date=19 September 2026}}</ref><ref name="si_mag"/> The winner of the competition qualifies for the play-off round of the [[2027–28 UEFA Conference League]].<ref>{{cite web |author=Winterburn, Sarah |title=How Premier League teams qualify for 2027/28 Champions League and Europa competitions |url=https://www.football365.com/news/how-premier-league-teams-qualify-for-2027-28-champions-league-and-europa-competitions |website=[[Football365|Football365.com]] |publisher=Planet Sport Ltd |date=19 September 2026 |access-date=20 September 2026}}</ref>

==Teams==
All 92 clubs in the Premier League and English Football League entered the season's EFL Cup.<ref name="all_clubs">{{cite web |title=EFL Cup second round: Premier League clubs' fixtures revealed |url=https://www.premierleague.com/en/news/4687523/efl-cup-second-round-premier-league-clubs-fixtures-revealed |publisher=Premier League |date=10 August 2026 |access-date=19 September 2026}}</ref> Access was distributed across the top 4 leagues of the [[English football league system]].

There was a preliminary round before the first one due to the number of teams participating in Europe. This round consisted of the two newly promoted sides to [[2026–27 EFL League Two|2026–27 League Two]] – [[York City F.C.|York City]] and [[Rochdale A.F.C.|Rochdale]] – and the two lowest finishers not relegated from [[2025–26 EFL League Two|2025–26 League Two]], [[Tranmere Rovers F.C.|Tranmere Rovers]] and [[Crawley Town F.C.|Crawley Town]].<ref name="York_Host">{{cite web |title=York host Crawley; Tranmere welcome Rochdale in EFL Cup |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/articles/clyp4648pe0o |website=bbc.com |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |date=3 June 2026 |access-date=4 June 2026}}</ref>

