==Rule changes==
The regulations governing the EFL Cup were amended ahead of the [[2025–26 EFL Cup|2025–26 season]] to allow, in certain circumstances, a player to represent two clubs during the same season’s competition.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Colman |first1=Jonty |last2=Kinsella |first2=Nizaar |title=Chelsea's Guiu eligible for EFL Cup after mix-up |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/articles/c89d12091qgo |work=BBC Sport |publisher=British Broadcasting Corporation |date=23 September 2025 |access-date=22 September 2026}}</ref>

Under those provisions, a player who [[Transfer (association football)|transferred]] before the first leg of the semi-final could represent their new club in the [[Two-legged tie|second leg]] and, if selected, the final. A transfer completed after the first leg, however, rendered the player ineligible for any further participation in that season's competition. As a result, they could not feature in the final should their new club reach it.

For the 2026–27 season, the regulations have been amended further. A player who transfers during the [[Transfer window|winter transfer window]] is now permitted to appear in the final for their new club, provided they satisfy the other eligibility criteria. They cannot, however, represent one club in the first leg of the semi-final and another in the second.<ref name="Key_Info"/>

There has also been a modest revision to the regulations concerning [[Loan (sports)#Association football|players on loan]]. From 2026–27, a player registered on loan is automatically eligible to participate in the EFL Cup for their loan club, unless their parent club expressly provides otherwise. Previously, loan players needed written permission from their parent club before they could take part in the competition.<ref name="Key_Info"/>

==Preliminary round==
The preliminary round was required for the 2026–27 EFL Cup following the participation of nine [[Premier League]] clubs in European competitions, equalling the Premier League record set the previous season.<ref>{{cite web |author=Coverdale, David|title=How Palace's UEFA Conference League triumph affects European qualification |url=https://www.premierleague.com/en/news/4671711/how-crystal-palace-uefa-conference-league-final-affects-european-qualification |publisher=Premier League |date=27 May 2026 |access-date=20 September 2026}}</ref> It featured the two clubs promoted from the [[National League (division)|National League]], York City and Rochdale, and the two clubs that finished 21st and 22nd respectively in the [[2025–26 EFL League Two|previous season's League Two]], Tranmere Rovers and Crawley Town.<ref name="York_Host"/> The round reduced the number of teams entering the subsequent rounds so that 32 clubs could participate in the third round, when the nine European qualifiers entered the competition.<ref name="Premlim_Round"/>

The draw was held on 3 June 2026, with Sanny Rudravajhala of Sky Sports hosting and former goalkeeper [[Lee Camp (footballer)|Lee Camp]] performing the draw.<ref name="Prelim_CFC">{{cite web |author=Johnson, Nick |title=Carabao Cup 2026/27 – Preliminary Draw |url=https://chesterfield-fc.co.uk/news/preliminary-carabao-cup-draw |website=chesterfield-fc.co.uk |publisher=Chesterfield F.C. |date=3 June 2026 |access-date=20 September 2026}}</ref> It paired newly promoted [[York City F.C.|York City]] with [[Crawley Town F.C.|Crawley Town]] at the [[York Community Stadium]], while [[Tranmere Rovers F.C.|Tranmere Rovers]] were handed [[home advantage]] against [[Rochdale A.F.C.|Rochdale]].<ref name="Prelim_CFC"/><ref name="Premlim_Round"/>

Tranmere Rovers and Rochdale contested the opening match of the preliminary round at [[Prenton Park]] on 1 August, drawing 2–2, with Rochdale winning the ensuing [[Penalty shoot-out (association football)|penalty shoot-out]] 2–1. [[Charlie Whitaker]] and [[Jordan Davies (footballer)|Jordan Davies]] scored for Tranmere, while [[Ryan East]] and [[Zain Silcott-Duberry]] replied for Rochdale.<ref name="Tranmere_Rochdale">{{cite web |title=Tranmere miss four penalties in cup exit to Rochdale |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/live/ce852vq2n1vt |website=bbc.com |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |date=1 August 2026 |accessdate=20 September 2026}}</ref> Rochdale missed their first two penalties but converted their next two, while Tranmere missed four of their attempts in succession after scoring their first, resulting in their elimination.<ref name="Tranmere_Rochdale"/> It was only the second EFL Cup meeting between the clubs, following Rochdale's 3–2 aggregate victory in the [[1987–88 Football League Cup#First round|1987–88 first round]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Tranmere Rovers football club: record v Rochdale |url=https://www.11v11.com/teams/tranmere-rovers/tab/opposingTeams/opposition/Rochdale/ |website=11v11 |accessdate=20 September 2026}}</ref>

In the other preliminary-round tie, York City lost 2–0 to Crawley Town on 3 August, with [[Gianmarco Di Biase]] opening the scoring before [[Danilo Orsi]] sealed the win from the penalty spot.<ref name="York_Crawley">{{cite web |title=Crawley win at York to set up Watford EFL Cup tie |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/live/cwyrx1xr7eet |website=bbc.com |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |date=3 August 2026 |accessdate=20 September 2026}}</ref> It marked York's return to the League Cup since 2015 and their first meeting with Crawley since the since the [[2015–16 Football League Two|2015–16 League Two]] campaign, when Crawley were unbeaten, winning one and drawing one.<ref>{{cite news |title=York City v Crawley Town pre match stat pack |url=https://www.efl.com/news/2026/august/03/york-city-v-crawley-town-pre-match-stat-pack/ |publisher=English Football League |date=3 August 2026 |accessdate=20 September 2026}}</ref> 

Having both advanced as the visiting side in their preliminary-round ties,<ref name="Premlim_Round"/><ref name="Key_Info">{{cite news |title=Carabao Cup 2026/27 - Key Information |url=https://www.efl.com/news/2026/august/06/carabao-cup-2026-27---key-information-/ |publisher=English Football League |date=6 August 2026 |accessdate=22 September 2026}}</ref> Rochdale and Crawley Town were drawn on the road in the first round but were eliminated by higher-division opposition, losing 2–0 to [[Bradford City A.F.C.|Bradford City]] and 1–0 to [[Watford F.C.|Watford]], respectively.<ref name="Round_One"/><ref>{{cite news |author=Murray, Scott |title=Carabao Cup first round: wins for West Ham, Burnley and Millwall – as it happened |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/live/2026/aug/08/west-ham-v-portsmouth-burnley-v-notts-county-carabao-cup-first-round-live |work=[[The Guardian]] |publisher=Guardian Media Group |date=8 August 2026 |access-date=20 September 2026}}</ref>

