==Second round==
A total of 46 teams played in the second round: 35 winners from the first round, and the 11 [[Premier League]] clubs not involved in European competitions.<ref name="all_clubs"/> The draw for this round was split on a geographical basis into northern and southern sections, where teams were drawn against a team from the same section. The draw was made on 10 August 2026, hosted by [[David Prutton]] and performed by [[Jobi McAnuff]] and [[Jamie Mackie]].<ref>{{cite news |title=Carabao Cup Round Two draw details confirmed |url=https://efl.com/news/2026/august/06/carabao-cup-round-two-draw-details-confirmed/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260809152852/https://www.efl.com/news/2026/august/06/carabao-cup-round-two-draw-details-confirmed/ |publisher=English Football League |date=6 August 2026 |access-date=8 August 2026 |archive-date=9 August 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Carabao Cup Round Two draw confirmed |url=https://www.efl.com/news/2026/august/10/carabao-cup-round-two-draw-confirmed/ |publisher=English Football League |date=10 August 2026 |access-date=20 September 2026}}</ref>

