==Third round==
32 teams played in the third round: the 23 second round winners, and the nine Premier League teams involved in European competition. The draw was made on 26 August 2026 by [[Jermaine Beckford]] and [[Jamie Redknapp]].<ref>{{cite news |title=Carabao Cup Round Three Draw: Anfield set to host Liverpool vs Tottenham |url=https://www.efl.com/news/2026/august/26/carabao-cup-round-three-draw--anfield-set-to-host-liverpool-vs-tottenham |publisher=English Football League |date=26 August 2026 |access-date=27 August 2026}}</ref>

In order to avoid scheduling issues, the eight clubs playing in the [[2026–27 UEFA Champions League|UEFA Champions League]] and [[2026–27 UEFA Europa League|UEFA Europa League]] could not be drawn against each other in the EFL Cup third round. There was a "pre-draw" to decide whether each of the eight clubs would play home or away. Eight clubs were then drawn from the remaining 24 to play against the eight Champions or Europa League sides. The remainder of the draw was open as usual.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.flashscore.com/news/all-you-need-to-know-about-the-efl-cup-draws-key-dates-teams-more/O2msMw0B/|title=All you need to know about the EFL Cup: Draws, key dates, teams & more|website=Flashscore|date=25 August 2026|access-date=26 August 2026}}</ref>

Six Premier League clubs were eliminated in the third round, with all six defeats coming against fellow top-flight opposition. Tottenham Hotspur, Manchester United and Leeds United were joined in exiting the competition by newly promoted [[Ipswich Town F.C.|Ipswich Town]], Hull City and Coventry City.<ref>{{cite magazine |author=Langell, Amanda |title=2026–27 Carabao Cup Fourth Round Draw: All Fixtures |url=https://www.si.com/soccer/2026-27-carabao-cup-fourth-round-draw-all-fixtures |magazine=[[Sports Illustrated]] |date=16 September 2026 |access-date=22 September 2026}}</ref> Fleetwood Town, the only [[EFL League Two|fourth-tier]] side to reach the third round,<ref>{{cite web |author=Varley, Sam |title=Preview: Fleetwood Town vs Sheffield United - prediction, team news, lineups |url=https://www.sportsmole.co.uk/football/fleetwood-town/league-cup/preview/fleetwood-vs-sheff-utd-prediction-team-news-lineups_605129.html |website=Sports Mole |date=14 September 2026 |access-date=22 September 2026}}</ref> recorded the round's biggest upset by defeating [[EFL Championship|Championship]] club [[Sheffield United F.C.
|Sheffield United]] 1-0, with goalkeeper [[Jay Lynch]] keeping his third clean sheet in as many EFL Cup matches this season.<ref>{{cite news |author=Statton, Kimberly |title=Fleetwood Stun Sheffield United to Make Carabao Cup History |url=https://thesportsencounter.com/2026/09/16/fleetwood-sheffield-united-1-0-carabao-cup-2026/ |publisher=The Sports Encounter |date=16 September 2026 |access-date=22 September 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |author=Brown, Findlay |title=Fleetwood Town vs Arsenal Carabao Cup tie given official date and kick-off time |url=https://uk.sports.yahoo.com/news/fleetwood-town-vs-arsenal-carabao-160933767.html |work=Yahoo Sports |publisher=Yahoo |date=18 September 2026 |access-date=22 September 2026}}</ref><ref name="clean_sheets"/>

[[Tottenham Hotspur F.C.|Tottenham Hotspur's]] difficult start to the season continued with a 3-1 defeat by Liverpool at [[Anfield]].<ref name="Pool_Spurs">{{cite news |author=Patel, Aadam |title=Liverpool 3-1 Tottenham: Dominik Szoboszlai stunner knocks Spurs out of Carabao Cup |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/live/cx980d6p7l20t |work=[[BBC Sport]] |publisher=British Broadcasting Corporation |date=15 September 2026 |access-date=22 September 2026}}</ref><ref name="Spurs_Diff>{{cite news |title=Teenager Dowman scores twice as Arsenal progress in League Cup |url=https://www.reuters.com/sports/soccer/teenager-dowman-scores-twice-arsenal-progress-league-cup-2026-09-15/ |work=[[Reuters]] |publisher=Thomson Reuters |date=15 September 2026 |access-date=22 September 2026}}</ref> [[Alexis Mac Allister]] and [[Cody Gakpo]] put Liverpool two goals ahead before [[Conor Gallagher]] reduced the deficit midway through the second-half, scoring Tottenham's first goal against Premier League opposition this season.<ref name="Pool_Spurs"/><ref name="Spurs_Diff/> [[Dominik Szoboszlai]] restored Liverpool's two-goal advantage in stoppage time with a long-range strike to send the 10-time winners into the fourth round.<ref name="Pool_Spurs"/><ref>{{cite news |author=Foster, Richard |title=The big League Cup final quiz |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/mar/21/big-league-cup-final-quiz-arsenal-manchester-city-wembley-sunday |work=The Guardian |publisher=Guardian Media Group |date=21 March 2026 |access-date=22 September 2026}}</ref>

The round also brought disappointment for [[Manchester United F.C.|Manchester United]],<ref>{{cite news |title=Michael Carrick shoulders blame for Manchester United's Carabao Cup collapse against Brighton |url=https://www.rte.ie/sport/soccer/2026/0916/1591837-carrick-shoulders-blame-for-uniteds-carabao-cup-collapse/ |work=[[RTÉ Sport]] |publisher=Raidió Teilifís Éireann |date=17 September 2026 |access-date=24 September 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |author=Jackson, Jamie |title=‘We can’t accept that’: Carrick urges Manchester United to respond after cup collapse |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/sep/16/michael-carrick-manchester-united-carabao-cup-third-round-defeat-brighton |work=[[The Guardian]] |publisher=Guardian News & Media |date=17 September 2026 |access-date=24 September 2026}}</ref> who after surrendering a two-goal lead against Brighton. [[Shea Lacey]] and [[Mason Mount]] gave United an early advantage, but Brighton responded through [[Charalampos Kostoulas]], [[Pascal Groß]] and [[Maxim De Cuyper]] to win 3-2.<ref>{{cite news |author=Ferridge, Arthur |title=Manchester United 2-3 Brighton: Red Devils suffer Carabao Cup heartbreak again after shock comeback |url=https://www.standard.co.uk/sport/football/man-utd-brighton-carabao-cup-b1297269.html |work=[[The Standard (London newspaper)|The Standard]] |publisher=Evening Standard Limited |date=16 September 2026 |access-date=22 September 2026}}</ref> It was the first time in 50 years that United had lost at home after leading by two goals.<ref>{{cite news |author=Baldwin, Alan |title=Man Utd out of League Cup after going 2-0 up at home and then losing 3-2 in 50-year first |url=https://www.reuters.com/sports/soccer/man-utd-out-league-cup-after-going-2-0-up-home-then-losing-3-2-50-year-first-2026-09-16/ |work=[[Reuters]] |publisher=Thomson Reuters |date=16 September 2026 |access-date=22 September 2026}}</ref>

In contrast, Chelsea produced a comeback of their own against Leeds United, recovering from 2-0 down to win 6-3 in a nine-goal contest, with eight of the nine goals coming after half-time.<ref>{{cite news |author=Arya, Yosua |title=Chaos at the Stamford Bridge! Cole Palmer inspires incredible Chelsea comeback as Leeds collapse in nine-goal Carabao Cup thriller |url=https://www.goal.com/en-gb/lists/chelsea-leeds-carabao-cup-nine-goals/blt39262f61875c8cac |work=[[Goal (website)|Goal]] |publisher=Integrated Media Company |date=9 September 2026 |access-date=22 September 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |author=O'Connor, Robert |title=Chelsea blitz Leeds with second-half comeback in Carabao Cup thriller |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/chelsea-leeds-carabao-cup-cole-palmer-b3047616.html |work=[[The Independent]] |publisher=Independent Digital News and Media |date=9 September 2026 |access-date=22 September 2026}}</ref> The match also marked the competitive debut of 16-year-old midfielder [[Reggie Watson]], son of former Premier League player [[Ben Watson (footballer, born July 1985)|Ben Watson]], who scored [[Wigan Athletic F.C.|Wigan Athletic's]] FA Cup final winner against Manchester City in [[2013 FA Cup final|2013]].<ref name="Watson_Chelsea">{{cite news |author=[[Agence France-Presse]] |title=Palmer, Rogers spark Chelsea's 6-goal spree in League Cup comeback |url=https://www.thescore.com/news/3595934/palmer-rogers-spark-chelseas-6-goal-spree-in-league-cup-comeback |work=theScore |publisher=Score Media and Gaming Inc. |date=9 September 2026 |access-date=22 September 2026}}</ref> Reggie became the fourth-youngest player to start a competitive match in [[Chelsea F.C.#History|Chelsea's history]] at the time of his debut.<ref name="Watson_Chelsea"/> [[Morgan Rogers]] was introduced at half-time and provided three<!-- DO NOT CHANGE: Sources, including Chelsea themselves, state that Rogers provided three assists. --> [[Assist (association football)|assists]] as Chelsea scored six times after the break to complete their comeback.<ref>{{cite web |author=Tear, Yann |title=Chelsea mount spectacular recovery via four half-time subs to see off Leeds United in Carabao Cup feast |url=https://www.capitalfootball.co.uk/single-post/chelsea-mount-spectacular-recovery-via-four-half-time-subs-to-see-off-leeds-united-in-carabao-cup-fe |website=Capital Football UK |date=18 September 2026 |access-date=22 September 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |author=Erluson, Brynjar Ingi |title=Taldi sig eiga verðlaunin skilið - „Ég lagði upp fjögur og hann skoraði úr víti!“ |url=https://www.fotbolti.net/news/09-09-2026/taldi-sig-eiga-verdlaunin-skilid-eg-lagdi-upp-fjogur-og-hann-skoradi-ur-viti |website=Fotbolti.net |language=Icelandic |date=9 September 2026 |access-date=22 September 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Analysis: How devastating Palmer and Rogers helped turn tie around |url=https://www.chelseafc.com/en/news/article/analysis-how-devastating-palmer-and-rogers-helped-turn-tie-around |website=chelseafc.com |publisher=Chelsea F.C. |date=10 September 2026 |access-date=22 September 2026}}</ref> 

[[Ryan Christie]] was another prominent individual performer in the third round, earning a nomination for the [[Carabao Energy Drink#Sponsorship|Carabao]] Cup Player of the Round.<ref>{{cite news |title='Here's hoping for a few more' - Christie |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/articles/c36ljzw054ro |work=BBC Sport |publisher=British Broadcasting Corporation |date=9 September 2026 |access-date=22 September 2026}}</ref><ref name="Round3_Noms">{{cite news |title=Vote for the Carabao Cup Player of the Round - Round Three |url=https://www.efl.com/news/2026/september/21/Vote-for-the-Carabao-Cup-Player-of-the-Round--Round-Three/ |publisher=English Football League |date=21 September 2026 |access-date=22 September 2026}}</ref> The Scottish midfielder scored three times in a 4-0 victory over Championship side [[Lincoln City F.C.|Lincoln City]], becoming the first Bournemouth player to achieve the feat in the League Cup.<ref name="Chrstie_Triple">{{cite news |author=Mitchener, Mark |title=Christie breaks new ground with hat-trick |url=https://sports.yahoo.com/articles/christie-breaks-ground-hat-trick-162430582.html |work=Yahoo Sports |publisher=Yahoo |date=9 September 2026 |access-date=22 September 2026}}</ref> It came in [[AFC Bournemouth|Bournemouth's]] 175th League Cup match since the competition began in 1960.<ref name="Chrstie_Triple"/>

Elsewhere, Everton advanced with a 1-0 victory over [[Wolverhampton Wanderers F.C.|Wolves]],<ref>{{cite news |author=Markham, Carl |title=Tyler Dibling's progression at Everton hailed as he shines in win over Wolves |url=https://www.irishnews.com/sport/soccer/tyler-diblings-progression-at-everton-hailed-as-he-shines-in-win-over-wolves-YQ2GLIFU6NII3D7AZ6SY5JQ2YM/ |work=[[The Irish News]] |publisher=The Irish News Ltd |date=16 September 2026 |access-date=24 September 2026}}</ref> while [[Coventry City F.C.|Coventry]] were defeated 3-1 by [[Aston Villa F.C.|Aston Villa]],<ref>{{cite news |title=Coventry 1-3 Aston Villa: What Lampard said |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/articles/c6vgy1jgjp8jo |work=[[BBC Sport]] |publisher=British Broadcasting Corporation |date=17 September 2026 |access-date=24 September 2026}}</ref> with [[Tammy Abraham]] scoring twice.<ref>{{cite web |author=Dawson, Jack |title=Nicolas Jackson facing Aston Villa axe after Unai Emery has mind made up for him |url=https://www.footballinsider247.com/aston-villa/match/nicolas-jackson-facing-aston-villa-axe-after-unai-emery-has-mind-made-up-for-him |website=Football Insider |publisher=[[Future plc]] |date=18 September 2026 |access-date=24 September 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |author=Fisher, Ben |title=Tammy Abraham's double powers Aston Villa to Carabao Cup win at Coventry |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/sep/16/coventry-aston-villa-carabao-cup-third-round-match-report |work=[[The Guardian]] |publisher=Guardian Media Group |date=16 September 2026 |access-date=24 September 2026}}</ref> [[Fulham F.C.|Fulham]] defeated West Ham 3-2,<ref>{{cite news |author=Steinberg, Jacob |title=Oscar Bobb takes Fulham past stubborn West Ham and into Carabao Cup last 16 |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/sep/15/west-ham-fulham-carabao-cup-third-round-match-report |work=[[The Guardian]] |publisher=Guardian Media Group |date=15 September 2026 |access-date=24 September 2026}}</ref> [[Brentford F.C.|Brentford]] beat Reading 2-1 and Peterborough United overcame Barnsley 7-6 on penalties after a 3-3 draw,<ref>{{cite news |author=Coates, Charlotte |title=Let them ref the games and be humans - Andrews |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/articles/cxj06nmjl3l6o |work=BBC Sport |publisher=British Broadcasting Corporation |date=15 September 2026 |access-date=24 September 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Peterborough United 3-3 Barnsley |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/live/c5x2zjpgwxlgt |work=BBC Sport |publisher=British Broadcasting Corporation |date=15 September 2026 |access-date=24 September 2026}}</ref> reaching the fourth round for the first time since [[2009–10 Football League Cup|2009]].<ref>{{cite news |title=Peterborough 3-3 Barnsley (7-6 on pens): Posh edge Carabao Cup third-round tie on penalties |url=https://www.skysports.com/football/news/13582702/peterborough-3-3-barnsley-7-6-on-pens-posh-edge-carabao-cup-third-round-tie-on-penalties |work=[[Sky Sports]] |publisher=Sky UK Limited |date=15 September 2026 |access-date=24 September 2026}}</ref> Manager [[Luke Williams (football manager)|Luke Williams]] oversaw the victory before being sacked four days later.<ref>{{cite news |author=Aloia, Andrew |title=Lowly Peterborough sack manager Williams |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/articles/crz6z7ypq6x8o |work=BBC Sport |publisher=British Broadcasting Corporation |date=19 September 2026 |access-date=24 September 2026}}</ref>

[[Crystal Palace F.C.|Crystal Palace]] defeated Middlesbrough 3-0,<ref>{{cite news |author=Tarling, Theo |title=Strand-Larsen brace sees Crystal Palace ease past Middlesbrough |url=https://www.london-now.co.uk/sport/26533621.strand-larsen-brace-sees-crystal-palace-ease-past-middlesbrough/ |work=London Now |publisher=Newsquest Media Group Ltd |date=8 September 2026 |access-date=24 September 2026}}</ref> with [[Jørgen Strand Larsen]] proving an aerial threat as he scored twice with [[Header (association football)|headers]] and was involved in all three goals,<ref name="Round3_Noms"/> setting up [[Daichi Kamada]] for the third.<ref name="Round3_Noms"/> Earlier in the round, Newcastle United, Sunderland and Bradford City had also secured victories.<ref>{{cite news |title=Carabao Cup round-up: Christie on fire, Toon slay Lions |url=https://www.rte.ie/sport/soccer/2026/0908/1590696-carabao-cup-round-up-christie-on-fire-toon-slay-lions/ |work=[[RTÉ Sport]] |publisher=Raidió Teilifís Éireann |date=8 September 2026 |access-date=24 September 2026}}</ref>

Arsenal also progressed, defeating Ipswich Town 4-2 at [[Portman Road]].<ref name="Dowman_Double>{{cite news |author=Herman, Martyn |title=Teenager Dowman scores twice as Arsenal progress in League Cup |url=https://www.reuters.com/sports/soccer/teenager-dowman-scores-twice-arsenal-progress-league-cup-2026-09-15/ |work=[[Reuters]] |publisher=Thomson Reuters |date=15 September 2026 |access-date=22 September 2026}}</ref> Sixteen-year-old [[Max Dowman]], a fellow nominee for the Carabao Cup Player of the Round, scored a brace for the Gunners, while [[Mikel Merino]] and [[Noni Madueke]] also found the net.<ref name="Dowman_Double/><ref name="Round3_Noms"/>

The final third-round fixture saw holders Manchester City begin their title defence with a 5-0 victory over [[Norwich City F.C.|Norwich City]] at the Etihad Stadium.<ref>{{cite web |author=Sharpe, Katharine |title=When is the EFL Cup fourth round draw? |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/articles/clyegmmvr4vo |work=BBC Sport |publisher=British Broadcasting Corporation |date=16 September 2026 |access-date=24 September 2026}}</ref><ref name="City_Start">{{cite news |author=Ojha, Chiranjit |title=Teenager Samba strikes twice on debut as Man City thrash Norwich in League Cup |url=https://www.reuters.com/sports/soccer/teenager-samba-strikes-twice-debut-man-city-thrash-norwich-league-cup-2026-09-18/ |work=[[Reuters]] |publisher=Thomson Reuters |date=18 September 2026 |access-date=22 September 2026}}</ref> Like Reggie Watson, 17-year-old [[Floyd Samba]] is the son of a former Premier League player, [[Christopher Samba]].<ref>{{cite news |author=Marshall, Tyrone |title=Man City's 'Mancunian' son of Premier League star lights up Youth League win |url=https://www.manchestereveningnews.co.uk/sport/football/man-citys-mancunian-son-premier-32504583 |work=[[Manchester Evening News]] |publisher=Reach plc |date=18 September 2025 |access-date=22 September 2026}}</ref><ref name="Watson_Chelsea"/> He scored twice on his senior debut, with [[Rayan Cherki]], fellow debutant [[Allan (footballer, born 2004)|Allan]] and [[Ryan McAidoo]] also finding the net.<ref>{{cite news |title=Man City teenager Floyd Samba scores 2 goals in 5-0 win over Norwich in League Cup |url=https://abcnews.com/Sports/wireStory/man-city-teenager-floyd-samba-scores-2-goals-5-0-win-over-norwich-league-cup-136541562 |work=[[ABC News (United States)|ABC News]] |publisher=ABC News Internet Ventures |date=18 September 2026 |access-date=22 September 2026}}</ref> City advanced to the fourth round, where they will face Brighton & Hove Albion.<ref name="City_Start"/> The two sides will meet again at the [[Etihad Stadium]] in the Premier League three days later.<ref>{{cite web |title=Manchester City scores & fixtures |url=https://www.skysports.com/manchester-city-scores-fixtures/2026-10-01 |website=[[Sky Sports]] |publisher=Sky UK Limited |access-date=22 September 2026}}</ref>

