==Fourth round==
The 16 third round winners were drawn to play each other in the fourth round. The draw took place on 16 September 2026, after the Manchester United vs Brighton & Hove Albion match concluded; [[Pien Meulensteen]] hosted the draw, while [[Jamie Redknapp]] and [[Ashley Young]] performed it.<ref name="round_four">{{cite news |url=https://efl.com/news/2026/september/08/carabao-cup-round-four-draw-details/ |title=Carabao Cup Round Four draw details |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260910042949/https://www.efl.com/news/2026/september/08/carabao-cup-round-four-draw-details/ |publisher=English Football League |access-date=8 September 2026 |archive-date=10 September 2026 }}</ref> The eight matches will take place in the week commencing 26 October 2026.<ref name="round_four"/><ref name="fleet_draw">{{cite news|url=https://www.efl.com/news/2026/september/16/carabao-cup-round-four-draw-in-full/ |title=Carabao Cup Round Four draw in full |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260916225715/https://www.efl.com/news/2026/september/16/carabao-cup-round-four-draw-in-full/ |publisher=English Football League |access-date=17 September 2026 |archive-date=16 September 2026 }}</ref>
 
Fleetwood Town are the sole League Two side remaining, reaching this stage of the competition for the first time in the club's history.<ref name="fleet_draw"/> Drawn against the defending Premier League champions, Fleetwood Town will host Arsenal at [[Highbury Stadium (Fleetwood)|Highbury Stadium]], which shares its name with [[Arsenal Stadium
| Arsenal's former home ground]].<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.beinsports.com/en-asia/football/league-cup/articles/arsenal-to-play-at-highbury-again-as-fleetwood-aim-for-efl-cup-giant-killing-2026-09-16 |title=Arsenal to play at Highbury again as Fleetwood aim for EFL Cup giant-killing |publisher=beIN Sports |date=16 September 2026  |access-date=17 September 2026}}</ref>

The League One meeting of Bradford City and Peterborough United features little League Cup history between the sides.<ref name="Posh_EFL">{{cite news |author=Swann, Alan |title=No luck for Peterborough United in the Carabao Cup draw, but history gives them a chance |url=https://www.peterboroughtoday.co.uk/sport/football/peterborough-united/no-luck-for-peterborough-united-in-the-carabao-cup-draw-but-history-gives-them-a-chance-9070563 |date=16 September 2026 |access-date=17 September 2026 |work=[[Peterborough Telegraph]]}}</ref> Posh have only faced Bradford once before in the competition during the [[1977–78 Football League Cup#First round|1977–78 opening round]], while this is the furthest the Bantams have progressed since reaching the [[2013 Football League Cup final|2013 final]] at Wembley.<ref name="Posh_EFL"/><ref>{{cite web |title=Bantams to host Peterborough in cup |url=https://www.bradfordcityafc.com/news/2026/september/16/bantams-to-host-peterborough-in-cup/ |date=16 September 2026 |access-date=17 September 2026 |website=bradfordcityafc.com |publisher=Bradford City}}</ref>

[[Xabi Alonso]] is set for his first return to Anfield as a manager outside of European competition, after Chelsea drew Liverpool in the fourth round.<ref name="Alonso_Return">{{cite news |author=Togher, Liam |title=When will Liverpool play Chelsea in Carabao Cup as fourth-round draw throws up familiar pairing |url=https://empireofthekop.com/2026/09/17/when-will-liverpool-play-chelsea-in-carabao-cup-fourth-round/ |date=17 September 2026 |access-date=17 September 2026 |website=empireofthekop.com }}</ref><ref name="fleet_draw"/> The tie marks the third time in six seasons that these two Premier League clubs have faced off in the EFL cup, having contested the [[2022 EFL Cup final|2022]] and [[2024 EFL Cup final|2024]] finals.<ref name="Alonso_Return"/>

The draw also features five other all-Premier League ties, with Everton handed a showdown against [[2025 EFL Cup final|2025 winners]] Newcastle as they bid to end a 31-year wait for domestic cup silverware.<ref>{{cite web |author=Bould, Guilia |title=Moyes' cup comments prompt fan questions |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/articles/c78058pjl95o |website=bbc.com |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |date=26 August 2026 |access-date=17 September 2026}}</ref><ref name="fleet_draw"/> Bournemouth and Aston Villa, meanwhile, will lock horns in the competition for the first time.<ref>{{cite web |title=AFC Bournemouth football club: record v Aston Villa |url=https://www.11v11.com/teams/afc-bournemouth/tab/opposingTeams/opposition/Aston%20Villa/#google_vignette |website=11v11.com |access-date=17 September 2026}}</ref><ref name="fleet_draw"/> The remaining fixtures include an all-London clash between Fulham and Crystal Palace, Brentford travelling to the [[Stadium of Light]] to take on Sunderland, while defending champions Manchester City will face Brighton.<ref name="fleet_draw"/>

